    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385-a7">

                <pb facs="0841" n="831" xml:id="pg831"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 9 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Acting Consul Cridland to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mobile,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> In a despatch dated the 26th June last
                    I had the honor to inform your lordship that the authorities at Richmond had
                    refused me permission to remain here till I could receive instructions from your
                    lordship with regard to the disposal of the archives of this consulate.</p>
                <p>On that same date, however, I again asked for the permission, stating that,
                    foreseeing the difficulty of obtaining instructions in the case from your
                    lordship, I had applied for the same to Earl Russell.</p>
                <p>I have received a reply from Mr. Benjamin, a copy of which I have forwarded to
                    Earl Russell, and now submit the same to your lordship.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRED J. CRIDLAND.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
